::ENG4_U06_PRE_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Unit 6 pretest scenario: A final project about career certification access must include oral explanation, digital slides, research support, multimedia publication, source credits, and an audience-ready sharing format. Which option is strongest? {
~A. Choose the option with the most decoration.#Incorrect. Decoration does not prove effectiveness. Unit 6 communication decisions should be based on purpose, credibility, accessibility, coherence, and audience needs.
=B. Present a focused claim with credible evidence and clear audience-centered organization.#Correct. This answer best applies Unit 6 communication skills with clear reasoning, evidence, audience awareness, and publication readiness.
~C. Use technical language without defining it for the audience.#Incorrect. Technical language must fit the audience. Define or explain terms when needed so the message remains clear and accessible.
~D. Share the product before checking source credits or accessibility.#Incorrect. Sharing before review can create credibility and access problems. Final communication should be checked for sources, usability, and audience readiness first.
}

